          "text": "Description: Testimony of an observation made in the spring of 2000 (no specific date, month, or hour: arbitrary date of 05/01/2000) and collected in 2008. One evening in the spring of 2000, a 13-year-old adolescent observed a red light on the living room wall that seemed to come from the outside. The witness then saw, for a few seconds, a stationary form behind a window that disappeared instantly. Only one testimony was collected. It is an unusable testimony by GEIPAN because the witness does not describe a PAN (aerospace phenomenon) but rather one or more lights on the ground or on a wall, with no possibility of linking it to a PAN as no PAN is described. The whole reported 8 or 9 years later, without a precise date. GEIPAN classifies this case as C: lack of information.",
